**How to implement.** The real explorer, composed beside the app's other shell seams (step 150: `ClockProvider.system` and `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow` live in `KitOpening.fs`). In `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`, beside `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow`, its doc one to three lines citing spec 0050 S5.3: `type ExplorerProxy with static member system : ExplorerProxy` (step 182). Its `showFolder folder` resolves the folder's text with `Path.GetFullPath`; a folder that does not exist (`Directory.Exists` answers false) answers `MissingFolderErr` naming it and starts nothing; otherwise it starts `explorer.exe` with the full path as its one argument (`ProcessStartInfo("explorer.exe")`, the path added through `ArgumentList`, `UseShellExecute` false), disposes the returned `Process` at once and answers `Ok ()`. Any exception of the resolution or the start is `ExplorerLaunchErr` carrying its message. It is the IO edge, in the shape of `KitFolderPicker.ofWindow`: nothing above it handles an exception, and it creates no folder, because a location that does not exist yet is told, never made (001 §G). No wait for the browser, retry or fallback browser is added. Tests: `ExplorerProxyTests` (step 182) gains `the system explorer refuses a folder that does not exist and starts nothing`: `ExplorerProxy.system`'s `showFolder` of a GUID-named folder under `Path.Combine(System.AppContext.BaseDirectory, "ExplorerProxyTests")` that the fact never creates answers `Error (MissingFolderErr _)` whose reason names that folder, and the folder still does not exist. No fact asks it to show a folder that exists, because that would open Explorer on the machine running the tests.

**Acceptance.** After the real explorer lands, `ExplorerProxy.system` MUST refuse a missing folder with `MissingFolderErr` and start Explorer only for a folder that exists; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the system explorer refuses a folder that does not exist and starts nothing`, the count rising by 1; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the fourteen s21 invariants MUST pass.
